        "original_id": "4ec08626-41bc-5a65-8b46-51e216caec3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Seminole leaders, Micanopy\n- Organizations: Seminole tribe, United States Government\n- Places: Indian Territory\n- Events: Second Seminole War\n- Concepts: Indian Territory, Indian country, Native American relocation\n\nFacts:\n- The Seminole leaders led between the time the Seminole tribe organized in the mid-18th century and the 1830s.\n- Micanopy and many Seminole were removed to Indian Territory in the 1830s following the Second Seminole War.\n- Indian Territory, the Indian Territories, and Indian country were general terms for an evolving land area set aside by the United States Government.\n- The United States Government set aside Indian Territory for the relocation of Native Americans who held aboriginal title to their land.",
